      "applicability": "not_applicable",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C58", "C61", "C63", "C64", "C65", "C66", "C67", "C68", "C69"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No human PK, dose, formulation, or prandial data for the query.",
    "L4 permeability/solubility records are for analogs (biperiden, trihexyphenidyl, fexofenadine, nicotine), not the query; transfer is analogical.",
    "First-pass metabolism and systemic clearance for the query are not directly measured; disopyramide's high F suggests limited first-pass for this scaffold, but this is not proven.",
    "Full ionization at pH 7.4 remains a possible absorption liability, though high-F comparators are also basic amines."
